# DEMO-NL-001 — a CUSTOM rule (not shipped with keur): flag Dutch prose in docs.
# Ships inside the demo dir so the tape is self-contained; load it by pointing
# KEUR_RULES_DIRS at docs/demo/rules (the sandbox passes it through).
#
# The point of the demo: your ESLint/Prettier/flake8 cannot do this. keur lets a
# team add a project-specific rule in ~10 lines that plugs into the SAME gate,
# verdict model and `keur learn` explainer as the built-in rules. English-only
# docs is a common house rule for shared/open repos; this enforces it.
id: DEMO-NL-001
ilities: [analysability]
maturity: 2
title: Dutch-language text in documentation (English-only house rule)
category: quality
severity: warning
engine: pattern
action: block
confidence: 0.9
target:
  extensions: .md
  exclude_paths: vendor/ node_modules/ .git/
patterns:
  # Common Dutch function words that don't collide with English. Word-boundary
  # anchored, case-insensitive. Deliberately small + high-signal to avoid false
  # positives on loanwords (data, via, …).
  - regex: (?i)\b(het|een|niet|werkt|deze|zijn|voor|met|gebruik|installeren|volgende)\b
    message: "Dutch text in a doc — this repo's docs are English-only. Translate the prose to English."
fix: "Write documentation in English. If a Dutch term is intentional (a proper name, a quote), suppress that line with 'keur:ignore DEMO-NL-001'."
